PRE-EXISTING ENVIRONMENT BLOCKER (full disclosure — NOT this change; NOT red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This slot's committed base tree (HEAD) does NOT compile — independently of this change. The Powershare
sibling (apple-page-charging-Powershare, 2026-06-14) built clean on the same Xcode 26.5; since then,
parallel P4-apple sibling phases committed breakage into this slot's tree. The page:system/TeslaAccount
sibling already recorded the same situation in apple-ledger.json (status=blocked, "Build blocked by
pre-existing MyActivityPage.swift errors"). Verified pre-existing via `git`: every file below is in HEAD
and UNMODIFIED by this change.

  A. Duplicate top-level types (parallel page-port vs widget-port both define the same name in one module):
       TirePressureUnit / TirePressureConvert / TirePressureStatus / TirePressureThresholds
         Features/VehicleSystems/TirePressureModels.swift  ⨯  dashboard-widgets/TirePressure*Widget.*
       (the widget TirePressureConvert uses `.fromSI`, the page one uses `.fromPascals` — incompatible,
        so they cannot simply be merged; resolving them means editing the sibling widget feature.)
  B. Access-control bugs in split sibling files (Swift 6.3):
       Sources/Features/Admin/DBHealthPage.Panels.swift  — 'model' inaccessible (private)
       Sources/Features/Admin/DBHealthPage.swift         — missing argument 'title'
       Sources/Features/System/DiagnosticPage.Sections.swift — many 'inaccessible due to fileprivate'
  C. Type errors in unrelated sibling code:
       Sources/Features/Dashboard/Widgets/BatteryRadialGaugeModel.swift — String? vs Int64?
       Sources/Features/System/NotFoundPage.swift — LocalizedStringKey vs String.LocalizationValue
  D. Xcode-26.5 SDK regression: the `#Preview` macro is ambiguous between SwiftUI.Preview and
       UIKit.Preview (iOS) / AppKit.Preview (macOS) in EVERY `#if DEBUG #Preview` block across the
       codebase (hundreds of files). Release config excludes them; a Debug build/`xcodebuild test`
       cannot compile the app host. (See apps/macos-pending-verifications.md.)

NONE of A–D is in ChargingCurve. They are out of this artifact's allowed-files scope and span unrelated
sibling features; resolving them would mean rewriting other agents' in-progress work. They are therefore
NOT fixed here. To PROVE the ChargingCurve code itself is clean despite the broken tree, three file-local
